{"name":"Pandanus","hex":"#616c44","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Pandanus","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Pandanaceae – palm-like, dioecious trees and shrubs native to the Old World tropics and subtropics; screw pines."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Pandanus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pandanus","blocks":[{"text":"Pandanus is a genus of monocots with about 578 accepted species. They are palm-like, dioecious trees and shrubs native to the Old World tropics and subtropics. Common names include pandan, screw palm and screw pine. The genus is classified in the order Pandanales, family Pandanaceae, and is the largest in the family."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Pandanus_utilis_fruit.JPG/330px-Pandanus_utilis_fruit.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pandanus","wikidata":"Q471914"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Pandanus_sp.2.jpg/500px-Pandanus_sp.2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Pandanus_sp.2.jpg/500px-Pandanus_sp.2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aerial, prop roots[5]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APandanus_sp.2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Naturalis_Biodiversity_Center_-_L.0939605_-_Aken%2C_J._van_-_Pandanus_repens_-_Artwork.jpeg/500px-Naturalis_Biodiversity_Center_-_L.0939605_-_Aken%2C_J._van_-_Pandanus_repens_-_Artwork.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Naturalis_Biodiversity_Center_-_L.0939605_-_Aken%2C_J._van_-_Pandanus_repens_-_Artwork.jpeg/500px-Naturalis_Biodiversity_Center_-_L.09396